# Project: Prescription (Rx) validator
Stack: Python 3, FastAPI, uvicorn, plain HTML + vanilla JS. pytest + httpx for tests.
No other dependencies. No frameworks on the frontend. No database.

## Source of truth
- docs/contract.md defines function signatures, request/response shapes, error codes. Follow it exactly.
- docs/assumptions.md defines domain rules. Do not invent new rules.

## File ownership (STRICT)
- Only create or edit the files your prompt assigns to you.
- If you need a change in another file, write it in docs/todo.md instead of editing.

## Code rules
- Never let an exception escape to the user. Bad input must become an error object.
- Error messages must name the eye, the field, the allowed range, and the received value.
- Collect all errors, do not stop at the first one.
- Keep it simple and readable. No clever abstractions.
- Float step checks must not use modulo; use round(v*4) comparison.

## Logging
- Append every non-obvious choice to docs/decisions.md as:
  "- [Agent X] <decision> because <reason>"
